# Adaptive expert cache (campaign expert-hot-set-lru): the GPU's expert slots
# follow the conversation, and the CPU tier's host bank follows Strata's RAM
# budget. Every mechanism is ported from Strata's source
# (github.com/Niko1221/Strata, written for this model on one GPU + RAM).
#
# MOE_CPU_TIER_ADAPTIVE=1 (over the static partition, patches 0018/0046):
#  - decode calls count each routed expert; every MOE_CPU_TIER_ADAPT_EVERY
#    decode steps (12) one swap batch is planned across all layers: decayed
#    counts (x0.7), candidates with usage >= 2.0, a swap only for a gain > 1.5,
#    the top MOE_CPU_TIER_ADAPT_SWAPS (96) by gain; no plan and no decay while
#    a swap is in flight (Strata src/program/generate.cpp:4413-4482). Policy in
#    adaptive_expert_cache.hpp.
#  - a swap hands the victim's pinned slot to the newcomer in place
#    (LRUCache::replace_pinned); nothing is ever evicted.
#  - non-blocking admission: a background reader reads and transposes the
#    newcomer from the file; the victim keeps serving until the bytes are
#    ready; then one copy is enqueued on the in-order compute queue with no
#    wait (after the victim's last readers, before the newcomer's first).
#    Deviation, recorded: Strata copies from its pinned arena on its own
#    stream.
#  - the RAM exchange: the newcomer's bank slot is re-keyed to the demoted
#    expert and read in the background (HostExpertBank::exchange), so the bank
#    keeps holding what the card does not (Strata
#    include/strata/core/expert_source.hpp:440-455). Deviation, recorded:
#    Strata copies the victim back from its GPU slot; this reads the file
#    (the slot's scales are in device layout).
#
# The RAM budget (Strata docs/DETAILS.md, engine 0.1.31):
#  - MOE_CPU_BANK_FIXED=1: the bank keeps its load-time set, changed only by
#    exchanges; a miss reads the file mapping through the page cache instead
#    of taking a slot by an O_DIRECT read.
#  - MOE_CPU_TIER_LOOKAHEAD=<file> (tools/export_router_lookahead.py): while
#    the tier works on layer L, a thread applies layer L+1's router to layer
#    L's MoE input, takes each token's top-k (MOE_CPU_TIER_LOOKAHEAD_K, 10) and
#    madvise(MADV_WILLNEED)s the predicted experts the card and the bank do
#    not hold (Strata src/core/expert_source.cpp:814-930). Pages only; the
#    experts computed are the same.
#
# Opt-in, not in the served configuration:
#  - MOE_CPU_BANK_PINNED=1: the bank as usm_host chunks
#    (MOE_CPU_BANK_CHUNK_MIB); O_DIRECT cannot target the driver's mapping
#    (every read failed), so the IO threads read through a bounce buffer.
#  - MOE_CPU_TIER_SPIN_US: the tier pool's workers and its waiter spin before
#    sleeping (within the spread at 2k tokens).
#
# Counters in [OTD_PERF]: adaptive plans/swaps planned/applied/dropped, the
# readers' time, bank exchanges, the lookahead's runs/skips/warmed experts,
# and decode-only GPU hits and tier join split by tier expert count and by
# bank-pending layers.
#
# Served gate (dense d48q8, B60, ratio 75 + census128, 15.4e9 device pool,
# 30 GiB host bank, 20,085-token needle, one fresh process per arm): static
# prefill 64.0 / needle decode 7.5 / 500-token decode 10.8 t/s; all of the
# above 65.5 / 10.3 / 12.4 t/s; needle right in both; window-0 KL against
# the f32 reference 0.577 vs 0.386, argmax 73.2 vs 81.5 % (inside the card's
# run-to-run floor; the answer-level bar is met).
#
# Files: adaptive_expert_cache.hpp (new), lru_cache.{hpp,cpp},
# expert_weight_providers.{hpp,cpp}, moe_otd_runtime.{hpp,cpp},
# moe_otd_perf.hpp, host_expert_bank.hpp, moe_3gemm_swiglu_opt.cpp,
# moe_cpu_expert.{hpp,cpp}, and the unit cells.

